<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan sugar output reaches 2.393 million T.</title>
<headline>Pakistan sugar output reaches 2.393 million T.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Monday sugar production had reached 2.393 million tonnes by June 30 compared to 2.47 million at the same time a year ago.</p>
<p>The mills had aimed to produce 2.4 million tonnes in 1996/97 (July-June) compared to the 2.47 million in 1995/96 and 3.0 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>Dealers bought 1.547 million tonnes, or 64.68 percent, of the production and the remainder was at the mills.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
